From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 024] panvk: expose multiViewport (maxViewports = 16)
Generated-by: LLM

Purpose: DXVK requires multiViewport. No exposed stage can write
 ViewportIndex (geometryShader = false, shaderOutputViewportIndex = false),
 so the viewport index of every primitive is 0 and the driver's use of
 viewports[0]/scissors[0] is the required behaviour. Pipelines and dynamic
 state with up to 16 viewports/scissors are accepted.
 Must be revisited when geometryShader or shaderOutputViewportIndex is
 exposed: per-primitive selection is then required (v10/v11 DCD has
 "Scissor array enable"; viewport transform is in the VS).
Source/Reference: Vulkan spec, ViewportIndex default 0; fork idea
 GunaCharanTeja a966c0d (multiViewport part only)
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (0xb8a31030, PAN_ARCH 11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Mesa base range: 5a07217f034b3e50d8c7c7794f97a2df1742613b
Dependencies: csf-v11/023
Validation test: tests/dxvk/vulkan/multi-viewport/multi_viewport.c (5/5 IDVS
 and PANVK_DEBUG=gpu_prerast)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c
index 85143c16371..b74f9f77ecc 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c
@@ -320,7 +320,7 @@ panvk_per_arch(get_physical_device_features)(
       .wideLines = true,
       .largePoints = true,
       .alphaToOne = false,
-      .multiViewport = false,
+      .multiViewport = PAN_ARCH >= 10,
       .samplerAnisotropy = true,
       .textureCompressionETC2 = has_texture_compression_etc2(device),
       .textureCompressionASTC_LDR = has_texture_compression_astc_ldr(device),
@@ -962,7 +962,7 @@ panvk_per_arch(get_physical_device_properties)(
       .maxDrawIndirectCount = PAN_ARCH >= 10 ? UINT32_MAX : 1,
       .maxSamplerLodBias = (float)INT16_MAX / 256.0f,
       .maxSamplerAnisotropy = 16,
-      .maxViewports = 1,
+      .maxViewports = PAN_ARCH >= 10 ? 16 : 1,
       .maxViewportDimensions = {MAX_FRAMEBUFFER_DIMENSION, MAX_FRAMEBUFFER_DIMENSION},
       .viewportBoundsRange = {-2.0f * MAX_FRAMEBUFFER_DIMENSION, 2.0f * MAX_FRAMEBUFFER_DIMENSION - 1.0f},
       .viewportSubPixelBits = 0,
